import importlib.util
from pathlib import Path
s=importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('bank',Path(__file__).with_name('build-bank.py')); m=importlib.util.module_from_spec(s);s.loader.exec_module(m)
extra=[]
def add(q,a,ref,n): extra.append((q,a,ref,n))
add('Which components and tracks are unlimited, what happens when a limited supply runs out, and what information is normally hidden?', 'Proxies allowed for cash, trophies/passed laws, dice and regiments; Balance/VP/Vote tracks unlimited. Other supplies limited, complete as much as possible. Everything public including discards except facedown blackmail (firm strategy/bid selection temporarily secret).','Rules p6 lines654–666; p40 lines2773–2789','Component exhaustion and information rules.')
add('What can be traded in negotiations and what cannot? How is a transferred share represented, and can blackmail be traded after use?', 'Can trade enterprises, facedown blackmail, family cash, shares and promises; not officeholders/writers/officers/prizes/spouses/passed laws/played blackmail/PM dial/trophies or Chairman piece. Replace share with recipient family piece. Played blackmail faceup and untradeable; unplayed can be peeked at but traded facedown. Adjust luxury VP ownership.','Rules p8 lines757–807','Legal asset transfers and ownership.')
add('Are immediate and future deals binding? What limits govern promise calling, simultaneous unfulfillable calls and repeated activation after a transfer?', 'Immediate transfers binding, future deals nonbinding. Printed promise card may force guarantor if able within card timing; may trade promises incl third party/guarantor. Cannot call during Final Scoring. Guarantor chooses which when simultaneous calls cannot all fulfilled. Transfer cannot activate resource twice, such as workshop bonus.','Rules p8 lines762–807; p9 lines843–847','Negotiation obligations and timing.')
add('How does setup use extra player cards for five or six players, distribute holdings, award starting luxury points and build the London display?', 'Add 3 extra setup cards at five or 6 at six, shuffle/deal evenly. Take all printed holdings; office member/card, share Court, writers/officers in indicated boxes, Commander slot (no card); ship per shipyard at listed sea zone or yard if unfitted. Starting luxury +2VP. Shuffle prestige/blackmail together display3, prestige up blackmail down; shuffle laws.','Rules pp4–5 lines335–388,416–433,453–477','Core setup procedures beyond card-specific figures.')
add('When does the game end and which phase is completed if failure occurs during Events in India or from legislation? Can promises or negotiations continue in Final Scoring?', 'Scenario final turn or Standing leftmost failure. Ordinarily immediate; Events-triggered failure finish Events; law-triggered failure finish vote. No negotiation/promises/blackmail during Final Scoring except explicit card permission.','Rules p9 lines836–853; p27 lines1897–1902; p29 lines2008–2012;p36 lines2586–2587','End timing and final-scoring freeze.')
add('Explain final Power sources, tied first and tied second awards, and how final victory ties are broken.', 'Enterprises incl prestige and Company shares by Power track (bottom two zero); passed laws and trophies +1 each, PM+2, applicable card power incl blackmail faceup/down and spouse. Most/second points based final turn board table; tied first each lower award only, no other award; tied second nothing. Final VP tie most windows then PM clockwise.','Rules p9 lines812–853','Power scoring sources and tie branches.')
add('How does Company survival versus failure affect shares, workshops and final retirements?', 'Survival add current Court VP per Company share and final office attrition/retire pensioners without prestige. Failure subtract same value per share, add1 per uninvested workshop, draw random failure card instead of normal final retirements. Scores can be negative. Firm special retirement is available regardless before these steps.','Rules pp9,37 lines829–835,2665–2674','Company outcome scoring branches.')
add('How do spouses affect transfers, restrictions and retirement discounts, and how often can a discount be used?', 'Spouse untransferable with permanent printed restriction; negotiate required trades immediately when taken. Discounts personal, stack, each usable once per London Season and once Final Scoring; reduce actual spending for prestige priority.','Rules p12 lines1018–1037','Spouse restrictions and discount timing.')
add('What happens to fitted ships if their shipyards are returned by Violet Effingham or a tax? Can someone buy those shipyards immediately?', 'Ships remain fitted/in play; returned shipyards cannot be purchased while matching ship in play. Losing luxury/prize removes its points when applicable.','Rules pp12,34 lines1022–1025,2344–2357','Orphaned fitted shipyards.')
add('List each family purchase/enlistment cost and immediate effect, including votes, income and failure scoring.', 'Writer one to Presidency (once-turn vacancy extra separate); officer one to Training. Luxury £4 bank,2VP while owned, social/window. Shipyard £2 bank matching unfitted ship, shipping,1vote,£1 bonus if fitted. Workshop £5 bank manufacturing,2votes,£1 bonus,1VP if Company fails unless invested. Seek Share printed empty space cost bank applicant.','Rules pp13–14 lines1100–1134','Family action menu exact costs.')
add('If a family must place a piece but has none in supply, what is required? What if no Family action is possible?', 'Must take from any own prize and lose its printed VP; also applies firm shares. If no action possible, no action and opportunity marker returns supply.','Rules p13 lines1083–1099','Forced cannibalization and no-action branch.')
add('What happens if a Chairman must be hired but the Court is empty, including if the former Chairman has no supply pieces or prizes?', 'Former Chairman automatically next, place member from supply or must use prize if possible with VP loss; if impossible there is no Chairman.','Rules p15 lines1191–1194; p13 lines1083–1085','Empty-Court fallback distinct from election deadlock.')
add('Who hires the Director, Shipping, Military Affairs, Presidents, Governors and China, and what candidate fallback restrictions apply?', 'Chairman hires Director from current officeholders except self/Governors, writer if all offices vacant; Shipping/China any writer. Military Affairs from Commander, if none officer, if none Training. Director hires President from own Presidency writer/Governor. President hires Governor from associated writer/officer, never Commander.','Rules p16 lines1234–1254','Specific hiring graph and fallback hierarchy.')
add('What can successful Special Envoys accomplish, can they repeat, and when may the Director transfer pieces?', '£1 treasury per die/no penalty, repeat envoys while able; success open closed non-Company order or create China with immediate Chairman writer hire. Then up to two transfers one writer/ship each between Presidencies/sea zones incl China.','Rules pp18,25 lines1417–1433,1808–1815','Envoy destinations and post-action transfers.')
add('In what order does Military Affairs transfer pieces, assign trainees and appoint Commanders? When is an incumbent replaced and does Nepotism apply?', 'Up to two officer/regiment Army transfers top half, then assign all trainees top half, then Commander vacancies or family with strictly more Army pieces than incumbent family triggers appointment among largest families. Previous Commander officer top half. Tie with incumbent preserves incumbent; no Nepotism.','Rules p19 lines1472–1520','Military ordering and incumbent-tie branch.')
add('Who orders Presidency actions, can Commander or Governors decline, can their actions be interrupted, and what may Chairman do with vacant President?', 'President orders own Trade/Commander/Governors, must give opportunity, Commander/Governors may decline. Each completes all actions before next; Trade before/after positions not interrupt. Vacant President Chairman chooses order but cannot trade/approve alliance purchases.','Rules p20 lines1527–1544','Presidency scheduling and vacant authority.')
add('Do trade ships become exhausted, and how do placed writers and Presidency dividers return during Refresh?', 'Trade capacity one order per ship, not Army-style exhaustion. Writers placed on routes return to associated Presidency, not arbitrary/home region writer box. Divider separates adjacent different-Presidency writers; tokens/dividers removed at Refresh.','Rules pp20–21,36 lines1555–1582,2612–2619','Trade identity across map and refresh.')
add('When are local alliances purchased and exhausted, who funds them, and can their strength be split or reused for Deploy and defense?', 'Commander requests at start own operations; President approves/pays printed cost from its treasury; move top. Each alliance used once in purchase turn for Deploy or defense, full strength unsplit; active alliances exhausted at Refresh, unlike officers/regiments reactivated.','Rules pp22,36 lines1617–1627,2618–2619','Temporary alliance lifecycle.')
add('When a Commander deploys into their own Company region solely to reopen orders or clear unrest, what dice penalty, loot minimum and trophies apply?', 'Company-controlled defending strength zero; deploy only if closed order/unrest. After loss check minimum loot surviving used officers+Commander (one each); zero tower means zero tower trophies; open all orders/clear unrest, no new Governorship.','Rules pp22–23 lines1630–1650,1674–1703','Successful suppression branch distinct from conquest.')
add('If a conquered capital was an empire and the Elephant pointed outward from the conquered region, what happens to flags and Elephant?', 'Remove target tower/dome and all matching empire flags; Elephant placed fully inside conquered region to threaten Company rebellion.','Rules p23 lines1693–1707','Conquest capital/Elephant consequences.')
add('How many successes does a Governor need to build a Company ship, where is it during construction and where does it go? How are Governor regiments treated?', 'Two build successes: ship in region initially with no other effect; next build success sends to associated Presidency sea zone. Regiment into associated Army, officer-like strength, bank takes its loot, no officer-loss rolls.','Rules p24 lines1753–1762','Governor production staging.')
add('What creates China, how is it hired, what resources does its treasury hold, when does it act and what ships count Eastern?', 'Envoy success or Envoy to China law, immediate Chairman hire any writer. Ship-only treasury, ships assigned/moved by Shipping/Director like sea zone. Acts after Bengal; ships Eastern for expenses/events/storms/laws.','Rules p25 lines1808–1816','China creation and zone identity.')
add('Can China repeat a failed trade check, trade with no export icons, or earn revenue from non-Company export icons? Give its dice, revenue and bonus.', 'Only one attempt, cannot attempt without export icons in Company regions, one die per ship. Success Balance£4 per export in all Company regions and Superintendent£1 each; non-Company exports not counted.','Rules p25 lines1817–1823','China attempt limits and controlled-export scope.')
add('What happens when Governor General law passes to Governors, incomplete ships, Director and fatigue? How are subsequent conquests and region losses different?', 'Governors pensioners, overlays and partial ships removed; no new Governors/overlays. Replace Director holder/card with GG preserving fatigue and treasury/turn; Governor/Director cards boxed. GG hires Presidents/hired like Director and normal attrition. Subsequent loss skips Governor elimination.','Rules p26 lines1841–1859','Governor General institutional transition.')
add('What guaranteed revenue does Governor General earn before Govern checks? Explain unrest from sixes, failure and tax, options per region and success limit.', 'Balance£3 per controlled region before checks. Treasury£1/die; every6 adds unrest every controlled region, unsuccessful adds further one each. Success personal£1 per region, must benefit once per region ship any sea inclChina/regiment anyArmy/tax£2 Balance or treasury except own; tax unrest different regions for multiple choices. One successful Govern max, failures retry while resources/noncatastrophic.','Rules p26 lines1860–1889','Govern action complete outcome rules.')
add('What is paid during Bonuses, and can an enterprise moved between players collect again that phase?', '£1 per fitted shipyard and uninvested workshop from bank; transfer cannot trigger twice.','Rules pp8,27,38 lines770–774,1894–1896,2719–2720','Bonus applicability and transfer suppression.')
add('How do storms affect unfatigued/fatigued player ships, Company/extra ships, China and firms?', 'Roll per affected player-owned ship;1–2 no change,3–4 fatigue or sink if fatigued,5–6 sink, return shipyard unfatigued. Company/extras exempt. China Eastern; firms strategy zone, Hobnob exempt.','Rules pp25,28,42 lines1813–1815,1943–1954,2919–2922','Storm outcome branches and zone exceptions.')
add('What happens when an event closes an order containing a writer or filled token, and how does a Cascade handle already closed connected orders and repeated regional flooding?', 'Writer supply; filled token flip closed. Fully closed source region cascades to connected orders; if target connected order already closed take northernmost open in that region; if none Cascade there. Each region initiates once per tile, may receive multiple effects.','Rules p28 lines1962–1975','Order closure and Cascade branching.')
add('How do Turmoil, Windfall and Shuffle identify locations and resolve? Include the empty-draw-stack Shuffle exception.', 'Turmoil northernmost open top-stack-region order or Cascade. Windfall£1 per writer on orders in top-stack region and adjacent regions. Shuffle March first, shuffle tile with remaining draw stack then shuffle discards onto top; empty draw stack March last.','Rules p31 lines2111–2123','Noncrisis event procedures.')
add('How does Leader differ in sovereign and dominated regions, and when does it move Elephant?', 'Top-stack sovereign region gains tower; dominated rebels with printed explosion modifier. March only when Elephant fully in Company region that successfully rebelled.','Rules p31 lines2124–2132','Leader branches.')
add('How does Peace differ with Elephant on a border versus fully within a region, and does it move afterward?', 'Border open connected orders across it, add tower each touched non-Company region. Fully within instead all local orders open and unrest removed. Then March.','Rules p31 lines2133–2139','Peace positional branches.')
add('In a non-Company Invasion, which strengths count, does equal strength win, how do flags change and what if no empire flags remain?', 'Attacker whole empire+modifier must strictly exceed defender whole empire. Success defender dominated flag; defender capital shatters old empire. Unflagged attacker creates capital/small flag if set available, if none no flags/new empire. Failure attacker -1 tower.','Rules p32 lines2192–2208','Invasion comparison and flag shortage.')
add('In a non-Company Rebellion, which empire regions count, what wins a tie and which side loses a tower on failure?', 'Only rebel and sovereign capital strengths; modifier attacker, strictly greater required so tie fails. Success remove rebel flag, close its open orders/Cascade if all closed. Failure removes tower from capital, not rebel.','Rules p32 lines2209–2219','Rebellion scope and failed-target exception.')
add('List Region Loss destinations, officer checks, loot status and Standing loss escalation. Do these losses remove other Company regions automatically?', 'Commander supply and half family trophies round up; officer die6 supply each in associated Army; Governor card unused, member/fatigue supply; remove overlay/partial ship/unrest; dome one tower appropriate invasion flag; token region loot-down, disassociate. Invasion close orders/Cascade; other attack types already do so. Standing first region-1 second-2 etc. Other regions not automatically lost; each resolves its attack.','Rules p29 lines1987–2012; p33 lines2262–2296','Full loss cleanup/escalation.')
add('How does Elephant March choose a region after successful Invasion versus other Marches, and its posture for Company, dominated, sovereign or fully formed empire?', 'Successful Invasion capital via Imperial Ambitions, otherwise top stack region. Company fully inside; dominated toward sovereign; sovereign shape border toward neighbor, skipping dominated neighbors clockwise. All neighbors dominated use redirect-arrow shape border toward capital.','Rules p30 lines2045–2082','Elephant priority and full-empire exception.')
add('How does Foreign Invasion select targets, calculate strength, alter towers/flags/orders and potentially redirect Elephant?', 'Storm die WestBombay/SouthMadras/EastBengal, all each, none top-stack. Die per target strength, Invasion/Company defense. Success close orders once/Cascade if all closed, remove flag/all if capital, Company dome restored, set strength half attack die rounded down. March circle only if Elephant fully in Company region invaded.','Rules p33 lines2297–2316; PDF p33 circle icon','Foreign Invasion targets and special outcome.')
add('When can PM stop drawing laws and how does a dilemma affect selection? How is the proposed policy chosen?', 'Reveal one at time up to3, can select earlier drawn and discard rest; dilemma forced/stop. Choose clockwise/counterclockwise, stop first matching law icon; policy includes target and consequence, arm moves before vote. Read law/set starting support.','Rules p34 lines2330–2343,2365–2367','Law selection and directional policy constraint.')
add('How do normal taxes, window taxes, bonuses and power policies work, including target already highest in Power track?', 'Tax£1 per target, return unpaid target inclChairman. Window additional cash for all windows on enterprises and prize members, return unaffordable enterprise/member. Bonus£1 per target. Power swap target next higher; target highest choose any other pair. Prestige enterprises count.','Rules pp3,12,34 lines115–119,1033–1037,2344–2364','Policy consequences and highest-power exception.')
add('How are votes bought and reused across rounds, who may call more rounds, and when must voting stop?', '£1 family per vote plus card icons once per vote by rotating cards; clockwise PM first. PM may call additional full rounds or stop after round; zero-vote round must resolve. Unlimited support track using counters. Restore used cards after vote.','Rules pp35–36 lines2525–2540,2584','Voting resources and round limits.')
add('Can a supporter later oppose, can an opponent later support, how is Opposition Leader selected and how do coalition votes and PM promise exceptions work?', 'Supporter may oppose later, opponent cannot support again in vote. Most opposition votes leader; incumbent tie retains. Consent permits votes for player already/committed opposing and count for their total. PM cannot oppose or consent enterprises but enterprises may be forced against by vote promise.','Rules p35 lines2541–2564','Opposition direction and coalition exceptions.')
add('Must final-turn prizes pay upkeep, what happens to unpaid prizes, and what exactly refreshes on nonfinal turns?', 'Pay each prize upkeep even final; unpaid member supply loseVP. Final skipRefresh scoring. Otherwise writers associatedPresidency; tokens/dividers/extras supply; officers/regiments active, active alliances exhausted; advanceTurn.','Rules p36 lines2602–2621','Upkeep/final-refresh exception.')
add('Explain the firm special retirement limit, eligible piece, dividend cap, spouse discounts, zero-marker restriction and Final Scoring timing.', 'One special per shareholder London Season from supply, not per firm, cash spent cap highest total marker among owned firms; absent/zero no eligibility. Discounts allow printed cost above cap. Normal retirement incl prestige except Final Scoring at start after firm scoring, regardlessCompany success/failure, no prestige.','Rules p37 lines2651–2674','Firm retirement distinct system.')
add('Where do firm investments/trade proceeds go, what pays ship fitting/bids, expenses and dividends, and may family cash be gifted into firms?', 'Investments London; trade India. London ship fitting/bids; expenses either; dividends India only; remaining India London after dividends. No family cash transfer to/from treasuries.','Rules pp37,39–42 lines2635–2647,2729–2739,2773–2779,2838,2888–2918','Treasury ringfencing.')
add('When is Firms phase and who resolves timing conflicts within or between firms?', 'After Family complete inclnew shares, before Hiring. Investments no set order until nobody wishes actions, then simultaneous strategies. Firmmanager resolves within firm, PM betweenfirms.','Rules p38 lines2679–2688; p40 lines2773–2775','Investment timing jurisdiction.')
add('May a firm fit another player’s ship without consent, buy Company or extra ships, or buy a player’s fitted Company ship? State costs and payment destinations.', 'Consent needed shipyardfit£3 bank. Cannot acquire Company/extras. Owner-consented fitted player ship buyback£3 unfatigued/£2 fatigued fromLondon toShippingtreasury.','Rules p39 lines2729–2740','Firm acquisition differs Company.')
add('What prerequisites allow hostile takeover, and what moves or stays the same?', 'Initiator not firmmanager, majority shareholder consent, not necessarily shareholder self. Move ships/cash/shares to initiator charter; copy value and dividend cubes; former board/cubes reset.','Rules p39 lines2741–2748','Takeover authority and continuity.')
add('What makes a merger legal, determines primary firm and handles over-ten shares? What happens to secondary treasuries and charters?', 'Every shareholder of all firms consents, primary highest value tied players choose. Negotiate sharetransfers; over10 returned only ownerconsent. Whole immediate agreementbinding. Consolidate all ships/shares/treasuries atprimary, secondarycharters family.','Rules p39 lines2749–2768','Merger unanimity and excess-share branch.')
add('What does Hobnob permit and forbid, what happens to its retirement marker and ships in storms, and must the firm still pay expenses?', 'No cash bid, no trade/no dividends, still pay expenses. Keep previous dividend marker rather than zero; ships exempt storms.','Rules pp40,42 lines2782–2785,2913–2922','Hobnob branch.')
add('Does a closed chosen home port prevent a firm selecting its strategy? When are bid and strategy revealed and how many checks can it attempt?', 'Closed home does not preventselection, musthave ship. Choose zone/home and Londonbid secretly, revealcash simultaneously but retaincarddown. Revealcard/checkatPresidencystart beforeactions, onceonly, cashpaidbank.','Rules p40 lines2773–2795','Strategy secrecy and closed-port branch.')
add('If no President successfully trades, when do successful firms fill orders and who breaks initiative ties? What if President does trade?', 'No presidentialtrade: afterCommander/Governors opportunity, Chairman breaksties. SuccessfulPresident: fill followingtradecheck in ascendinginitiative, Presidentbreaksties. Initiative each shipcount minussuccessdice1/2.','Rules p40 lines2791–2809','Firm resolution fallback.')
add('If multiple firms or Company refill the same open order, what is paid, can one firm fill it twice and what is required for its route?', 'Alreadyfilledbyother actor pays halfprinted valuerounddown. One firm once perorder; open connectedroute fromstrategyhome throughits ownfilledorders; maxships+1. Company can refill firmorders, not override normal route/homeprivilege restrictions. FirmrevenueIndia/value+1per£6.','Rules p40 lines2810–2822; pp20–21 lines1555–1582','Shared order market and own-route constraint.')
add('Can a firm at ten shares still receive emergency investment? What resources may be invested, what happens to its Value and unused rescue cash, and does same-turn-share restriction persist?', 'Yes,no newsharesatcap. Same eligibleCompanyshare/workshop procedure, managerconsent; immatureCompanysharesstillnotusable/weakshare restrictionpersists. Payexpenses, unusedcashlost, Value-1spaceperinvestment.','Rules pp38,41 lines2689–2724,2845–2850','Emergency rescue restrictions.')
add('How does emergency merger differ from a normal multi-firm merger and whose expenses must be paid?', 'Facing dissolution canmergewithoneother, negotiated shareholderconsent pernormalrules. Otherfirmfirstpaysownexpensesifnotalreadypaid and outstandingendangeredfirmexpenses.','Rules pp39,41 lines2749–2768,2852–2855','Emergency merger timing and limit.')
add('What must shareholders consent to for voluntary dissolution and where do its shares and ships go? Do invested workshops recover?', 'Allshareholdersconsent. Usesdissolution: sharesDebtorsPrison-1VP, shipsmatchingyards, charterfamily; workshopsremaininvested.','Rules pp37,41 lines2648–2650,2839–2843','Voluntary dissolution consent and irreversible costs.')
add('Can shareholders waive firm dividends, is manager paid an extra amount, how is retirement capacity recorded and what becomes of retained India cash?', 'EachdividendIndiaonly£1pershareplus£1manager. Waiveanynumberofownsharesperdividendwithmanagerconsent. Recordtotalactualcashpaid marker; nonHobnobnopayoutzero, Hobnobkeepold. RestIndiaLondon.','Rules p42 lines2888–2918','Dividend waiver and marker basis.')
add('How are firm shares and Debtor’s Prison scored relative to ordinary final scoring, including fractional points and Company failure?', 'Atstartscore/loseprintedfirmVPpershare; DebtorsPrison-1piece; totalfractionalVP thenrounddown. Thenoneeligiblespecialretirement regardlessCompanysurvival; thennormalPower/Court/finalretirementorfailure.','Rules p37 lines2665–2674; p41 lines2839–2843','Firm final scoring order and fraction handling.')
# Reject drafts that add no distinct rule beyond fixed earlier entries.
rejected_novelties={'Conquest capital/Elephant consequences.','Bonus applicability and transfer suppression.','Strategy secrecy and closed-port branch.','Firm resolution fallback.','Shared order market and own-route constraint.','Dividend waiver and marker basis.'}
rejected=[e for e in extra if e[3] in rejected_novelties]
extra=[e for e in extra if e[3] not in rejected_novelties]
add('What are the cost, upkeep, VP and windows of each of the five prizes?', 'Cost/upkeep/VP/windows: £2/0/0/0; £4/£1/2/1; £8/£2/4/2; £14/£3/8/3; £20/£4/12/4. Per family member on prize.','Official PNP Board page1; supplements/images/board-left-details.png','Printed prize values not stated numerically in rules text.')
add('Which turns do 1710, 1758, 1813 and Long 1710 start and finish, and which include deregulation?', '1710 turns1–5 monopoly withoutderegulation;1758 turns3–7 mayderegulate;1813 turns5–8 startsderegulated;Long1710 turns1–8 mayderegulate.','Rules p4; Official PNP Board page1; research-notes.md','Scenario lengths and scope.')
add('What are 1710 and 1758 initial Standing, Debt, treasury funds, passed laws, regiments and Company ships, including 1758 control token?', '1710 £10expectations,Debt0,£3eachtreasury,RoyalProtection,oneRegimentperArmy,noCompanyships.1758 £12expectations,Debt3,£4each,CalicoActs,oneRegimentperArmy,oneCompanyshipEast,BengalcontroltokenBengalPresidency.','Official PNP Bridge Fronts p9 cards74–75; official errata setup','Earlier scenario numeric setup.')
add('What changes are required for 1813 setup: initial finance/laws/military/ships, Company share value, Governor General, China and control tokens?', '£10expectations,Debt0,£3eachTreasury;MilitaryOversight,DeregulationDebtorsPrisonside,CalicoActs;2regimentseachArmy,1Companyshipeachzone;+2/-2sharetokenCourt;GovernorGeneralLAWboxed,overlayreplacesDirector,Chinaofficecreated,threehomecontroltokensmatchingPresidencies.','Official PNP Bridge Fronts p9 card76; full-official-errata.txt','1813 numeric setup and incorporated corrections.')
add('What Power awards apply to final turns 1–3, 4–6 and 7–8, and what happens to a tied-first group in each?', 'First/second3/1,5/2,8/4respectively. Tiedfirsteachloweraward1/2/4only,nootheraward.','Rules p9; Official PNP Board p1; images/board-left-details.png','Printed final-turn power award values.')
add('What are initial Power positions and which Standing/Debt spaces permit or force a Deregulation vote? Where is S?', 'Social2,Companyshare1,shipping/manufacturing0. Standingexpectations£4/6/8lined,Debt5–8lined;Standing£4orDebt8starforcesvote. S£10expectations.','Official PNP Board p1; Rules p36','Printed power/deregulation thresholds.')
add('According to the verified designer ruling, does unrest increase a Foreign Invasion primary attack or its resulting tower strength? What happens to orders?', 'Neither. Primaryattackordinarydieonly,resultingtowerfloor(die/2);normalCompanysecondaryunrestattacksstillapply. Onsuccessorderscloseonce/Cascadeonlyifalreadyclosed.','Cole Wehrle 2023-04-30 BGG article42192767; supplements/foreign-invasion-designer-ruling.json; Rules p33','Official designer exception to normal Crisis unrest; source conflict recorded separately.')
add('Which corrected card rules apply when Mercantile/Diplomatic Connection reduces dice to zero, Company Fraud would overdraw Balance, Public Demands Impeachment removes a holder, or Military Oversight demotes a Commander?', 'ConnectionszeroDicefailure;FraudstartRevenue,twicehighestofficeholderrollreduceBalanceminzero,takethatcashbank;Impeachmentholdersupply/cardVacantOffices;demotedCommanderisofficerandeligibleforreappointment.','full-official-errata.txt cardcorrections; official PNP Bridge Fronts','Applicable card errata not normal rules.')
if __name__=='__main__': m.bank('expanded-v1',m.seed+extra)

